# Hard to fix — recall and store

Owner notes live in **`ODDTROVE-CAPABILITIES.md`** → section **“Hard to fix right now (owner notes for Cursor)”**.

## When the owner asks what’s hard to fix

Phrases like **“what’s hard to fix?”**, **“what can’t cursor fix?”**, **“pull up hard to fix notes”**:

1. Read that section in `ODDTROVE-CAPABILITIES.md`.
2. Reply in plain English — short list, no code unless they ask.
3. Do **not** start a build in that turn unless they pivot to a new task.

## When the owner asks to store a note

Phrases like **“remember this as hard to fix”**, **“log that cursor can’t fix X”**, **“add to hard to fix”**:

1. Append a dated bullet under that section (what failed or is blocked; why in a second line if helpful).
2. Skip if the same point is already there unless they want it updated.
3. Confirm in chat that it was saved.

This section is **owner-maintained pain log**, not product roadmap — use site roadmaps for “not built yet” features.
